title: The Chemnitz Conference
subtitle: The signal for the rising is to be given at a workers' conference.
new-page: true
tags: rf_event
view-if: year = 1923 and month >= 10 and saxony_seen = 1
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.chemnitz_seen = 1;
Q.october_leader = Q.leader;
Q.october_leader_name = window.RF.names[Q.leader];
!}

= The Chemnitz Conference

On 21 October a conference of factory councils, unions and workers' parties meets in Chemnitz. The plan is for the KPD to propose a general strike there, as the signal for the rising. Without the left SPD, the strike will be a Communist affair alone.

[? if spd_relation >= 55 : The left SPD delegates are listening. Some of them might follow. ?][? if spd_relation < 55 : The SPD delegates, led by Labour Minister Georg Graupe, make clear they will walk out if the KPD proposes a general strike. ?]

[? if october_plan = 0 : Moscow's plan was postponed, but the question of a strike is on the agenda anyway. ?]

Readiness: [+ readiness +]. Revolutionary situation: [+ rev_situation +]. Union influence: [+ union_influence +].

- @call_strike: Call the general strike.
- @retreat: Withdraw the proposal. Live to fight another day.
- @demand: Demand that the leadership call the strike.
- @accept_retreat: Back a retreat.

@call_strike
view-if: player_leads = 1
on-arrival: chemnitz_strike = 1
go-to: rising

@retreat
view-if: player_leads = 1
on-arrival: chemnitz_strike = 0
go-to: retreated

@demand
view-if: player_leads = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.strike_pressure += 2;
Q[Q.player + '_strength'] += 2;
!}
go-to: leader_decides

@accept_retreat
view-if: player_leads = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.strike_pressure -= 2;
Q[Q.player + '_moscow'] -= 3;
!}
go-to: leader_decides

@leader_decides
on-arrival: {!
var p = Q.strike_pressure;
var strike = 0;
if (Q.leader == 'right') { strike = p >= 4 ? 1 : 0; }
else if (Q.leader == 'left') { strike = 1; }
else if (Q.leader == 'center') { strike = (Q.rev_situation >= 75 && p >= 2) ? 1 : 0; }
else if (Q.leader == 'stalin') { strike = Q.october_plan; }
Q.chemnitz_strike = strike;
!}
go-to: rising if chemnitz_strike = 1; retreated if chemnitz_strike = 0

@rising
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.rising_won = window.RF.rising(Q) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: won if rising_won = 1; crushed if rising_won = 0

@won
on-arrival: rf_over = 1; rf_ending = "revolution"

= The general strike

The conference votes for the general strike. Saxony and Thuringia stop. The Proletarian Hundreds take the police stations and arsenals the plan named. In Berlin, the Ruhr and Hamburg the factories empty, and enough of the SPD's members come out that their leaders cannot hold them back. When the Reichswehr marches on Saxony, it finds railwaymen who will not move its trains and soldiers who will not shoot.

(Rising: [+ rising_score +] against the [+ rising_needed +] needed.)

@crushed
on-arrival: {!
Q.october_outcome = 'crushed';
Q.members = Math.round(Q.members * 0.6);
Q.readiness = 0;
Q.repression += 40;
Q.spd_relation -= 15;
Q.union_influence -= 15;
Q.rev_situation -= 25;
Q.party_banned = 1;
Q[Q.leader + '_moscow'] -= 10;
!}

= The rising fails

The strike is called, but the SPD workers stay at work. Where the Hundreds rise, they are isolated in a few towns. The Reichswehr moves into Saxony and Thuringia. Within days the leaders are arrested or in hiding, the party offices are closed, and the government bans the KPD.

(Rising: [+ rising_score +] against the [+ rising_needed +] needed.)

@retreated
on-arrival: october_outcome = "retreat"

= The retreat

The KPD withdraws its proposal. The conference refers the question to a commission, which is a polite way of burying it. Couriers are sent across the country to call off the rising.
